    "title": "Owensboro teen charged as adult in murder case - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ian Young ,\n1 hours ago\nHENDERSON, Ky. (WEHT) — A teenager charged in a deadly shooting earlier this year is now being tried as an adult.\nThat shooting happened in the 500 block of Orchard Street on March 13. A 17-year-old was arrested and charged in the case.\nTate Swanagan was in court Wednesday. A grand jury indicted him to be tried as an adult.\nPolice arrest 17-year-old in Owensboro juvenile’s murder Prosecutors say he turns 18 later this month and will be moved from a juvenile detention center to the Daviess County Jail. He’s accused of shooting and killing 17‑year old Jamarious Butler in March.\nAnother victim had serious injuries. Swanagan is charged with murder, first degree assault and tampering with physical evidence.\nHe’s being held on a $1,000,000 cash bond.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
    "summary": "HENDERSON, Ky. (WEHT) — A teenager charged in a deadly shooting earlier this year is now being tried as an adult. That shooting happened in the 500 block of Orchard Street on March 13. Police arrest 17-year-old in Owensboro juvenile’s murder Prosecutors say he turns 18 later this month and will be moved from a juvenile detention center to the Daviess County Jail. He’s accused of shooting and killing 17‑year old Jamarious Butler in March. Swanagan is charged with murder, first degree assault and tampering with physical evidence.",
